From 13b5f1f2d019ccd672457fa655eca764f632450c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:02:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/61] docs: correct partial-moment and central-tendency man
 pages

Roxygen sources (R/*.R, src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp + R/RcppExports.R)
and the committed Rd files are edited together:
- NNS.mode / NNS.gravity: discrete = FALSE is for continuous
  distributions (the text said discrete); NNS.mode returns a vector of
  modes with the default multi = TRUE.
- LPM.ratio, UPM.ratio, Co.LPM, Co.UPM, D.LPM, D.UPM, PM.matrix: the
  targets have no default; NULL selects the mean(s).
- PM.matrix: pop_adj is the n/(n-1) adjustment and is ignored when
  either degree is 0 (verified: identical output).
- NNS.moments: population = TRUE is the unadjusted statistic, FALSE the
  sample-adjusted one.
- NNS.CDF: $Function is an NNS.data.frame, not a data.table.
- UPM.ratio: replace the invalid \dontrun plot3d example.
- Co.LPM_nD / Co.UPM_nD / DPM_nD: norm divides by CLPM + CUPM + DPM at
  the same degree/target (verified 0.0567/(0.0567+0.0253+0.3355) =
  0.1358 = norm output) and has no effect at degree 0.
- LPM.VaR / UPM.VaR: degree 0 is the type-7 interpolated quantile.
Documentation only; no results change.
